{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,8,17]],"date-time":"2026-08-17T14:39:05Z","timestamp":1786977545807,"version":"build-2736575974"},"reference-count":50,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"12","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,13]],"date-time":"2024-11-13T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1731456000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":["aces.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["ChemNanoMat"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    High surface area porous activated carbons obtained from sustainable biomass are excellent functional materials for energy storage applications. This is the first report on snake gourd (Trichosanthes cucumerina) pericarp as a raw material of activated carbon and supercapacitor electrode material. Herein, a simple KOH activation and carbonisation method is used. The obtained SGC900 sample has a surface area of 1841\u2005m\n                    <jats:sup>2<\/jats:sup>\n                    \/g and an average pore volume of 0.52\u2005cm\n                    <jats:sup>3<\/jats:sup>\n                    \/g. SGC900 based supercapacitor exhibits good electrochemical storage capacity in 1\u2005M H\n                    <jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub>\n                    SO\n                    <jats:sub>4<\/jats:sub>\n                    with a specific capacitance of 206\u2005F\/g at 1\u2005A\/g. The symmetric device delivered an energy density of 11\u2005Wh\/kg at a power density of 1.6\u2005kW\/kg. It provides a series resistance (R\n                    <jats:sub>s<\/jats:sub>\n                    ) of 1.2\u2005\u03a9 and a charge transfer resistance R\n                    <jats:sub>ct<\/jats:sub>\n                    of 1.9\u2005\u03a9. Furthermore, the device retains 95\u2009% of capacitance over 5000 cycles. This work presents an easy and feasible approach for producing value\u2010added activated carbon from sustainable biomass, potentially used in high\u2010performance energy storage.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/cnma.202400112","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,15]],"date-time":"2024-10-15T13:03:49Z","timestamp":1728997429000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["Trichosanthes Cucumerina Derived Activated Carbon: The Potential Electrode material for High Energy Symmetric Supercapacitor"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"10","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0005-1965-6645","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Anit","family":"Joseph","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Metallurgical and Materials Engineering Indian Institute of Technology Madras  Chennai 600036 India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Arshitha","family":"Mathew","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Metallurgical and Materials Engineering Indian Institute of Technology Madras  Chennai 600036 India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-8322-6387","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Tiju","family":"Thomas","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Metallurgical and Materials Engineering Indian Institute of Technology Madras  Chennai 600036 India"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,11,13]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_7_1_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/j.matdes.2022.111017"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_2_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/nmat2297"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_3_1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1002\/adma.200903328"},{"key":"e_1_2_7_4_1","doi-asserte